domain VT102:
  description "Resume accepted immutable V3 battle binding on the existing cc304 worktree."
evidence USER:
  "The owner requested resuming work from the latest commit handoff on 2026-09-30."
evidence LOCAL:
  |
    The existing cc304 worktree is clean at 4a898d0 and matches its fetched remote.
    Its handoff explicitly names vt102 resume. Accepted requirement R2, ADR0039
    D1 and design v2 require frozen V3 generation identity and V4 compiler inputs.
    Current battle creation still parses V2 envelopes. Archived 77ed6a0 provides
    incomplete V4 work with type escapes; it is evidence, not a conforming delivery.
premise SCOPE:
  |
    Resume vt102 locally, preserving main and all other work. No new branch,
    provider call, Stage operation, push, deployment or upstream decision change.
    Reuse canonical PERT and measure actual resume time. Verify authority hashes
    and consumer boundaries before implementing; keep lifecycle deletion in vt110.
premise FIT:
  "The handoff continuation remains necessary and within the requested resumption."
pending COVERAGE:
  "Exact remaining consumer gaps and required implementation effort remain to be measured."
premise COPY:
  "Copy archived changes wholesale; rejected because current contracts differ and archived casts evade contract checking."
premise ADAPT:
  "Adapt the archived binding to accepted current contracts and verify each real consumer."
decision RESUME based_on USER, LOCAL, SCOPE, FIT:
  |
    Verify accepted file identities, resume vt102 via guarded perttool mutation,
    inventory frozen input consumers, then implement typed V4 binding and tests.
    Report remaining whole-game gates separately and retain measured uncertainty.
